<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6799"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 09, 2005 - 8:49 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;Pity about poor Catherine. Tick tock,&#34; said Anythony Hopkins in <i>Silence Of The Lambs.</i> This line has been used in parodic fashion in entertainment snippets ever since. I don&#39;t know that this is the real BTK posting, or if the &#34;tick tock&#34; references the film, but if so his stealing the material of someone else certainly fits. ;&#41;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
