<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6808"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 09, 2005 - 10:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Susan Peters was the obvious person that came to mind when I read that post and I mentioned it overtly once then and again as an aside, in a less obvious way by mentioning that camera men and technitians at local TV stations cannot be ruled out if theoriginal DNA specimens from BTK were false plants. I&#39;m sure that someone, who knows her, has noticed all of the recent &#34;heads&#39; up&#34;, and she has taken appropriate measures. <BR> <BR>The day after his posting there was some banter about some talk on the chat line which had spilled onto the message board. One of the posters, when speaking to &#39;the alledged BTK&#39; signed their post Susan. taBTK may have been referring to a conversation on the chat line. <BR> <BR>The &#39;rooster crowing&#39; and the &#39;tick tock&#39; referenses are so well-worn in prose and poetry that I went with my first impressions &#40;passing time&#41;&#40;rural, morning&#41;. <BR> <BR>THE MOST IMPORTANT LITERARY ALLUSION, I believe ,is the &#34;oh Anna&#34; poem. If anyone has found ANY additional info on that, please post it. <BR> <BR>This is one piece of confirmed BTK evidence that the public has available to us, that the police HAVE ASKED for our help on, that may shed some light on the case. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
