<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7168"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Richerich<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Richerich<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 12, 2005 - 3:41 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Amateur slueths notwithstanding, some of these posts are nonetheless very interesting. As such without useful info from LE....speculation runs rampant thruout these message posts. Reading far fetched implications into every minute detail from A to Z leads one to understand why LE does not let loose with details from their investigations. Btk is probably fascinated and amused by all the details written that are so far off the wall that he wonders when the time will actually come when someone whether in LE or the public trip him up in to being caught. Until then when LE have the evidence to make an arrest or he is tripped up in public communicating, then BTK is safe from apphrehension. unfortunately insulated by armchair uninformed detectives that read farfetched innuendo into every last piece of info whether authenticated or not. Being critical of my opinion is irrelevant. I have not nor will I use random speculation about the case but depend on the facts be them as they are gleaned from the professional investigators and what they choose to release to the public. I would imagine LE types close to the case keep the pertinent info non public for reasons that all these so called detectives could not understand. I do not claim to understand either, but common sense dictates to me LE is not withholding pertinent info just for grins to prolong the investigation, but to keep the public informed while tightening the noose around any suspects they may have. and one last thought: I will not ever believe LE would cover up a SK just because the family had money or influence. In my mind that again is absolutely, insanely, hysterically, preposterous. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7168-->
<!--Post: 7171--><!--Time: 1108255192-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7171"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Fsu44<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Fsu44<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 12, 2005 - 4:39 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hold on everyone, Richerich does have some very valid points. Before we threw him off this moving train, he has only regurgitated information known to many of us about how and why WPD has not released information to the public. The fact of the matter is that we are just going over known information from so many ports in an idly and often inconclusively manner. Richerich has just voiced his own personal opinion by attacking &#34;some&#34; of the posting. We have to agree that some of the ideas &#40;few&#41; are a bit silly. Let&#39;s not kill the messager. I rather have Richerich insight, keeps us on our toes. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7171-->
<!--Post: 7174--><!--Time: 1108258195-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7174"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 12, 2005 - 5:29 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hey, everyone here knows that I&#39;m the first one to call someone on a theory that has gone off the deep end &#40;alien babies with no dna, chimera, BTK is female, etc.&#41;. We have disagreements but most posters here are specific about which topics - they think - have crossed the line of basic common sense.  <BR> <BR>And I agree, sometimes someone has to say, &#34;Woah, tap the brakes sherlock&#34; but geez! <BR> <BR>If I could find one post from rich guy that would allow us to analyze his theories - and pick them apart if appropriate - then it would be different. <BR> <BR>Bring &#39;em! This is a tough, smart crowd. If they&#39;re so good, let&#39;s hear them.?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7174-->
<!--Post: 7176--><!--Time: 1108259487-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7176"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iq<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iq<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 12, 2005 - 5:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rich- <BR> <BR>Glad to see you&#39;re putting that thesaurus to good use. Now, start paying attention in english class and you may be able to use those words in the proper grammatical context. <BR> <BR>Although I do concede that a few of the revelations posted have been nothing but pure, unadulterated, fiction and/or speculation. In most cases, these posts are not represented as anything different. When it comes to this type of statement, each of us has a decision to make. We can choose to disregard the &#34;theory&#34; or we can elect to accept is as a &#34;plausible theory&#34;, but a &#34;theory&#34; nonetheless. We can then share these ideas with others that are familiar with the facts and discredit or substantiate them with feedback. Instead of taking this path, you simply choose to ridicule &#34;out of the box&#34; thinking.  <BR> <BR>You have grossly misinterpreted the presentation of therories in this forum. Ninety-nine percent of all BTK discussion is non-factual, we don&#39;t know enough about him to even have a factual discussion. However, if you are under the impression that LE doesn&#39;t have the same type of conversations amongst themselves, you are sadly mistaken. If you think that presenting information about a cold case to the public and asking for their help is a waste of time and man power, try telling that to the folks at &#34;AMW&#34;. <BR> <BR>If you are looking for a BTK discussion based completely in fact, maybe you should park your &#34;authenticated&#34; ass on the history page and talk to yourself. <BR> <BR>Before you post another pathetic rant, take the time to identify the &#34;far fetched implications&#34; you are referring to and their authors. <BR> <BR>Thank you, <BR> <BR>iq <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7176-->
<!--Post: 7178--><!--Time: 1108260354-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7178"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Fsu44<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Fsu44<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 12, 2005 - 6:05 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Lilymarie; I have never seen a posting from Richerich other than his last two, that being said; you have always been a sintinel. You have been here much longer than I, so I yeild to you and your bravdo. Which is a good thing <IMG SRC="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/clipart/happy.gif" ALT=":-&#41;" BORDER=0> <!--/Text--></td></tr>
