<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7180"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 12, 2005 - 6:38 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks, Fsu44. I just read IQ&#39;s post - which was articulated much better than mine.  <BR> <BR>There is, obviously a &#34;balance&#34; between the theories that are a bit &#34;out there&#34; &#40;those that tip to the right&#41; - and theories that rely only on the known &#34;facts&#34; &#40;the left&#41;. <BR> <BR>But we all respect those that are willing to put their own opinions, brainpower and skills to the task and take the heat in return.  <BR> <BR>I think we all have a problem with those that only criticize - especially with a huge dose of sarcasm - and do not add a single original thought.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7180-->
<!--Post: 7187--><!--Time: 1108266830-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7187"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 12, 2005 - 7:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I, beeing one of the posters here who come up with several of the &#34;tip to the right&#34; as Lilymari call them theories, would like to add that I belive that the strength of a &#34;team&#34; as the one we have here on catchbtk.com is actually that we are thinking and working SO differntly.  <BR> <BR>I belive that maybe in one of my wilder theories one of the more fact minded postes could use part of somthing I post, wich then might fit with somthing of the more factuel evidence. And in the best case scenario somthing new comes up, somthing I couldn´t put together and neither the &#34;factual&#34; poster could put together on ouer own, but because of the MIX of different thinking a new possible angle to the case is born? <BR> <BR>IMO it is NOT, &#34;one way or the other&#34; it is both ways that is the core of creative sleuthing. <BR> <BR>Thanks to all the positive posters! you are great!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7187-->
<!--Post: 7190--><!--Time: 1108267967-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7190"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 12, 2005 - 8:12 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Frankly, my whole &#34;theory&#34;, appearing right before Richerich&#39;s first remark was rather tongue-in-cheek. I realize that new posters are expecting some serious investigatin&#39;, and that to them outlandish=not serious. And I would refer them to the &#34;GENERAL DISCUSSION&#34; or &#34;THEORIES&#34; sections. In &#34;FEEDBACK ON MESSAGES TO/FROM BTK&#34; about all you can do is speculate on what may/maynot be a clue from someone who may/maynot be BTK. <BR> <BR>Facts really don&#39;t apply.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7190-->
<!--Post: 7199--><!--Time: 1108272380-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7199"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Richerich<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Richerich<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 12, 2005 - 9:26 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Posters: Criticize me, my grammar, anything else you so chose. It does not one way or another sway my pragmatic view of these or any other details thought of or gleaned from info released from LE. Common sense in LE practice depends on the evidence and circumstances presented from factual and thorough examination of what has been gathered. I neither criticize nor endorse some of the postings or the posters themselves. My opinion is that only..... mine. I am not trying to impart my thoughts or opinions on anyone. These out of the box rationale&#39;s and various musings founded on speculation and SWAG&#39;s are merely opinions given by the various posters who think they may have something LE havent thought of. Again LE are privy to info all posters probably cannot imagine. LE probably has the handle on whats really happening, but is waiting for the opportunity to make things relly happen.  I would like to think that after 30&#43; years LE will not blow the whole case on some petty technicality. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7199-->
<!--Post: 7205--><!--Time: 1108275076-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7205"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 12, 2005 - 10:11 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Skov - I hope that you didn&#39;t misunderstand - and take my right vs. left balance theory as a criticism. I respect your research &#40;you are an international google master-seriously&#41; as much or more than most. <BR> <BR>We sometimes come down hard on people that have a theory that we don&#39;t agree with - but with all due respect - they have actually brought a new thought, idea or twist that didn&#39;t exist before. <BR> <BR>What is difficult to take - is someone who comes here with nothing - and is critical of everything.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
