<!--Post: 7280--><!--Time: 1108353313-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7280"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Freya<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Freya<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 13, 2005 - 7:55 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rich, I gotta say, after reading all of the previous posts--and I generally like the other people who posted--I absolutely agree that as a registered poster, you have the right to express what you think about the theories posted here without being accused of being BTK himself. I also agree with the points you made about what will ultimately lead to a break in this case: police work. On the other hand, you undermined your own point about preposterous &#40;and I interpret that to also mean &#34;frivolous&#34;&#41; posts by posting several in which you repeated yourself. It&#39;s true that some people who post here get very sensitive about their theories, which is strange b/c they are putting them out there in the first place. But it seems illogical for you to both stress the incredibly unimportant role this forum plays in the capture of BTK, and then chastise even the most out-there posters for expressing their opinions here. If one follows your logic, then who cares how serious or ridiculous the theories are? Well, I don&#39;t, and I hope you continue to post, because I think your input is important.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7280-->
<!--Post: 7295--><!--Time: 1108375403-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7295"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 14, 2005 - 2:03 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yes, Rich, please feel welcome to stay. <BR> <BR>Anyway, now I have a question for everybody, but especially for you &#40;the realist&#41;.  In regard to both the &#34;known&#34; BTK and the guy posting as BTK, what is your read on their true intellect&#40;s&#41;?  Is either one capable of &#34;novel thinking&#34; as this guy is saying, which I&#39;m taking to mean that he might actually invent something in the arts, sciences, or public arena - or is he just blowing smoke?  I know we don&#39;t have much to work with.  And I don&#39;t care how annoying he sounds in his posts, or how much you hate his crimes - I just want to know how smart he is.  Maybe he&#39;s smarter than all of us - individually.  I&#39;m not afraid to admit it, if it&#39;s true.  You see, I&#39;m struggling to figure out what this guy&#39;s talking about, and I have a fairly decent and not-overly-speculative hypothesis going - but it would require him to show the sort of novel thinking that is required of a really good post-graduate student, or an entrepreneur, a true artist/designer, or even a professor.  But like you, I&#39;m also a bit of a realist.  If this guy isn&#39;t capable, then forget it.  Wasted brain cells, and I don&#39;t even care to post it.  So what&#39;s your read on BTK?  Is he capable of inventive, &#34;research-level&#34; stuff?  Or is it just kaka?  I no longer trust my own opinion on this, and I need a reality check.  I welcome all opinions, but especially opinions that stir up the facts a bit.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
