<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7328"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tadpole<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tadpole<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 14, 2005 - 9:55 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I can see your point Richerich, and it&#39;s good of you to post your opinion. I would imagine that if BTK is ever caught there will be many people who will be in disbelief because of his ability to blend in with the norm. <BR> <BR>It&#39;s good that everyone can put their thoughts out to others, sometimes I think people may overlook the obvious because they are looking to make something complicated.  <BR>  <BR>If the communication IS coming from the real BTK, and he IF does feel bad about the &#39;monster&#39; who made him do this, a deal to turn himself in might be possible in exchange for studies of what causes those monsters to take over. He would not only be known for his years of avoiding capture, but also for contributing to the scientific world. Of course, that&#39;s just my opinion.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
