<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7419"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Zenith<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Zenith<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 9:54 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m pretty disappointed that a number of the recent posts have turned into finger pointing and basically an online fight.  <BR> <BR>First of all, this discussion area is about BTK, not about others. Secondly, everyone should be free to express their ideas, thoughts and opinions. If someone thinks an idea you&#39;ve posted is ridiculous, so what? Everyone&#39;s going to differ on that opinion. But you&#39;ve got the right to post them and they&#39;ve got the right to state that they seem ridiculous. I think we all need to be a little more thick skinned.  <BR> <BR>If someone calls one of my posts ridiculous, or in this case preposterous, I would not retaliate by accusing them of being a &#34;From BTK&#34; poster or by pummeling them in return with all kinds of negative messages. Suffice it to say, &#34;Thank you for your opinion&#34;, and then take the feedback to heart or leave it, and go on with posting your thoughts about BTK. If someone hurts my feelings, suffice it to say, &#34;You hurt my feelings, did you intend to do that?&#34; <BR> <BR>A good rule to live by: You cannot create better behavior in others by being misbehaved yourself. <BR> <BR>This site is about BTK, not us. Let&#39;s get on with it.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7419-->
<!--Post: 7427--><!--Time: 1108492808-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7427"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Yomama<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Yomama<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 10:40 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->i am new here and i guess i should explain why i acused the poster that got some people mad...i have been reading  the posts on this board for quit awhile and  then i decided to regester and was waiting to get aproved to post and i was realy getting into what scov was posting and then she got upset and left...that upset me ...but to move forward i know i&#39;ve got alot to learn. i did listen to the recording of btk yesterday and i can&#39;t get out of my mind that he sounds like a cop...has this been explored at all here???  just checking<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7427-->
<!--Post: 7456--><!--Time: 1108505399-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7456"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 2:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Good rules to live by for adults &#40;not &#34;misbehaved&#34; children&#41;: <BR> <BR>1. New posters: READ THE SITE. ALL OF IT. Then, when you have a topic you want to explore - use the &#34;search&#34; tool to see if it already has a thread - and if your idea has been explored. <BR>2. PLEASE add your ideas &#40;search this site first&#41;. We need NEW ideas. Expand on the ones that are already here. <BR>3. You don&#39;t get much credit for criticizing other&#39;s ideas if you don&#39;t contribute anything yourself. Just using this board as a punching bag will get you the kind of reaction you see above. You should expect it - don&#39;t be surprised by it. You deserve it. <BR>4. Speaking of agendas - don&#39;t use this board to further your own personal/political/religious ones. Most posters here really have a desire to catch this awful abomination of nature. <BR> <BR>Just my 2 cents...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
