<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7489"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 5:35 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Lilymarie wrote on Saturday, February 12, 2005 - 5:29 pm:      <BR> <BR><font color="ff0000">Hey, everyone here knows that I&#39;m the first one to call someone on a theory that has gone off the deep end &#40;alien babies with no dna, <b>chimera</b>, BTK is female, etc.&#41;.</font> <BR> <BR>I think I was the first one to advance that idea, and it is the more plausible of the ones you mention, especially since chimeras are medically documented, and it might explain how BTK can leave DNA behind and yet not match a DNA test &#40;assuming he&#39;s been swabbed&#41;. <BR> <BR>The 4 points you mention are good advice for the newbies; however, the thing to remember is this site &#40;especially the message board&#41; is growing in leaps and bounds.  There are over 100 new posts every day, and many of them are mini-novels, so it is a lot to wade through.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7489-->
<!--Post: 7493--><!--Time: 1108519697-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7493"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 6:08 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m sorry, Ed. You&#39;re right. I read again, your thread on chimera, and I realize that I closed that off before I should have. Accept my apology, please? <BR> <BR>To clarify about reading the board - what I meant was Tom&#39;s work on the history, letters, voice recording and basic profiles of the victims. Reading these first would answer many of the new poster&#39;s questions.  <BR> <BR>I think it&#39;s a good idea to &#34;search&#34; the posts before posting if you&#39;re new because the odds are good that someone has opened it up and it&#39;s been researched by a whole lot of smart people already. And if not, then posting something new is always exciting for everybody. <BR> <BR>Lily <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7493-->
