<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7561"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Freya<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Freya<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 10:23 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Zenith, thanks for your post. I totally agree with you, but you wrote it more eloquently than I did.  <BR>  I didn&#39;t intend to post on this thread again until I read some of the posts after mine. I can&#39;t believe that I attempted to give constructive criticism to a poster who left some admittedly obnoxious but valid messages and received feedback that impliedly I and others were kissing that poster&#39;s butt and groveling.  <BR>  How hypocritical.  <BR>  I very much appreciate and admire the level of detailed analysis Skov has contributed to this board, but I equally respect another&#39;s option to call her theories preposterous. How is that wrong?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
