<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7940"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nancydrew<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nancydrew<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 1:10 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Do you guys on the &#34;messages to btk&#34; thread think that he&#39;s going to read it and just take your suggestion?  Do you imagine him sitting at his computer and saying, &#34;Oh, turn myself in and tell my story, great idea,&#34; or &#34;Hmmmm...Get a lawyer, why didn&#39;t I think of that?&#34; <BR>Even better, do you picture him breaking a sweat because you&#39;re telling him that you&#39;re on to him?   <BR>And if you do beleive he&#39;s reading it, what about those who insult and provoke him?  Why would you stir up a hornets&#39; nest? <BR>Sorry to be a smart aleck, but after 31 years, I don&#39;t think any of us have much influence over what he does next.  I&#39;m really not trying to be nasty about it.    <BR>Begging forgiveness in advance for my sarcasm.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
