<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7989"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Richerich<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Richerich<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 4:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I believe LE is closing in on the killer with some sort of LE trap being slowly but surely laid before him. I tend to think LE with the resources they exercise are luring  him into a false sense of superiority. He&#39;s always believed his cunning and luck elevates him above investigative techniques employed by LE. I&#39;ve recently noticed different postures from the media and LE in the precise and effective communicative messages they are delivering now thru the electronic media. It appears each carefully chosen and worded statement is tailored to echo a calm and resolute attitude from the media, much like some reverse psych ploy. Thruout all the message posts we read and contribute to, the murderer is either portrayed as having genius level intelligence on one end of a scale to rock dwelling roaches on the other end. Simply stated, the physcopath has thru the years eluded justice only thru attention to his own environment, keeping his cards close to his vest  and lots of luck. Think of him as the ultimate gambler............but eventually his luck like that of any common criminal, is soon to leave him............... <!--/Text--></td></tr>
