<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10513"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsbarn<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsbarn<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 3:35 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><a href="http://cdn.news.aol.com/aolnews_photos/02/07/20050302223609990003" target=_top>http://cdn.news.aol.com/aolnews_photos/02/07/20050 302223609990003</a> <BR> <BR>The string of letters and numbers above was supposedly sent in a letter to the Wichita Eagle &#40;March 2004&#41;, although I can&#39;t find it verified anywhere. This puts me in mind of the strings in the From BTK thread. <BR> <BR>Perhaps some sleuths will try to figure out those last two strings from this board &#40;I think the first one was successfully solved&#41;. I haven&#39;t been able to. <BR> <BR>The Eagle posters have noted the Texas/restless post may go back to the Raidar posting here who said he was from Texas.  <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
